          "text": "The change is in place:\n\n```python\ndef _make_keys_list(\n    secret_key: str | bytes | cabc.Iterable[str] | cabc.Iterable[bytes],\n) -> list[bytes]:\n    if isinstance(secret_key, (str, bytes)):\n        return [want_bytes(secret_key)]\n\n    keys = [want_bytes(s) for s in secret_key]  # pyright: ignore\n\n    if not keys:\n        raise ValueError(\"Must provide at least one secret key.\")\n\n    return keys\n```\n\nThis covers:\n- Empty lists `[]`, empty tuples `()`, one-shot iterators `iter([])` → ValueError immediately at Signer construction (also Serializer, via shared helper).\n- Individual string and bytes keys, including `\"\"` and `b\"\"`, still accepted via the isinstance branch.\n- Nonempty collections still work.\n- Signing/verification/tamper rejection/rotation untouched.\n\nThe change is minimal. I'm done — submit.",
